# Which test suites use the shared framework, and which still carry a case
# runner of their own.
#
# tests/testlib.ps is the one place a case that may raise is run, and the
# one place that puts the world back afterwards. A suite asks for it with
# `%!testlib` on its first line; run-ps-test.sh prepends it to those and to
# nothing else, because some suites here assert that a program's own
# dictionary starts empty or count the dictionary stack, and six read their
# own source through currentfile.
#
# This file is the list of suites that have NOT moved yet, with the shapes
# each one's own runner takes -- which is what a conversion has to preserve
# if the move is to be checked by diffing the suite's output rather than by
# reading it. The list is held to the tree in BOTH directions: a suite that
# grows its own runner and is not named here fails, and a name here whose
# suite no longer has one fails too. So the list can only shrink, and it
# shrinks by conversion rather than by editing.
#
# The guard also refuses the one mistake that would undo all of this: a
# suite that asks for the framework and then defines one of its names
# anyway. That shadows the shared runner with a local one silently, which
# is exactly the arrangement that let a false pass sit in a hundred and
# forty-six files.
#
#   own <suite>  <helper>[ <helper>...]

